# Copy this file to .env (which is gitignored) and fill in the two values below.
# The same two variables must also be set as secrets in the Cloudflare deploy; see
# "Warcraft Logs setup" in README.md.
#
# Warcraft Logs API client, created at https://www.warcraftlogs.com/api/clients/
#   - Name: something descriptive, e.g. "The Lionhearts guild website (thelionhearts.eu)".
#     The API terms let Warcraft Logs cancel a client whose owner or use is unclear.
#   - Redirect URL: https://thelionhearts.eu/ (the form requires one, but the client
#     credentials flow used here never redirects).
#   - Leave "Public Client" unchecked. A public client gets no secret and can only use
#     the PKCE flow, which cannot reach the /api/v2/client endpoint this site uses.
#
# Never commit real values: this repository is public, and the API terms forbid
# embedding credentials in open source projects.

NUXT_WCL_CLIENT_ID=
NUXT_WCL_CLIENT_SECRET=
